\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  O for a thousand tongues, to sing
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 My great Redeemer's praise,
\par The glories of my God and King,
\par The triumphs of his grace!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  Jesus! The name that charms our fears,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 That bids our sorrows cease;
\par 'tis music in the sinner's ears,
\par 'tis life, and health, and peace.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  He breaks the power of cancelled sin,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 He sets the prisoner free;
\par His blood can make the foulest clean,
\par His blood availed for me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He speaks, and, listening to his voice,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 New life the dead receive,
\par The mournful, broken hearts rejoice,
\par The humble poor believe.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Hear him, ye deaf; his praise, ye dumb,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Your loosened tongues employ;
\par  Ye blind, behold your Saviour come;
\par And leap, ye lame, for joy!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.  My gracious Master and my God,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Assist me to proclaim,
\par To spread through all the earth abroad
\par \pard     The honours of thy name.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

